penguins and crushingly high g-forces  don't mix or at least they shouldn't but  in the batman the penguin escapes a  brush with death a little too easily  let's talk about that scene spoilers for  the batman ahead when the batman kicks  off bruce wayne has been patrolling  gotham for two years he's already  cemented himself as a brutal force on  the streets and he's created a sense of  paranoia in the city's criminal element  so whenever they see a symbol in the sky  they know he could strike from the  shadows at any moment he's a savage  fighter as seen in the film's opening  sequence with the skull-faced thugs who  target a passenger on the subway but  bruce isn't just up against petty  criminals in the 2022 film he's also  investigating a terrifying serial killer  called the riddler who goes after  corruption at the highest levels of  civil authority yes that's a strangely  heroic cause for a murderer who  terrorizes his victims with bizarre  traps and explosive collars gotham has  plenty of room for more than one  costumed vigilante since the city is  full to the brim with other criminals  it's not so surprising that the dark  knight meets some other iconic  characters over the course of the movie  chief among them is selena kyle aka  catwoman who is really more of an  anti-hero than a proper villain another  villain is notorious crime boss carmine  falcone who sits at the heart of  gotham's underworld last but certainly  not least is the charismatic oswald  cobblepot aka penguin a gangster who's  pulled into batman's investigation into  the riddler the penguin has quite a few  meaty scenes in matt reeve's first  batman flick but one of those scenes  doesn't really make any sense  one of the biggest action sequences of  the film sees batman chase the penguin  in a high-speed pursuit down the gotham  freeway after he suspects the mobster of  being an informant for the gcpd the  dramatic scene causes plenty of chaos on  the road and gives fans a look at what  the new batmobile is capable of it's one  of the best action sequences in the  entire film with the cinematography  dropping the audience right in the  middle of the swerving vehicles batman  even uses a ruined truck to ramp through  an explosion like a real comic book hero  and when he plows into penguin's car the  crash that results is brutal with the  mobster's vehicle spinning violently  through the air before he lands upside  down cabo pod is trapped in his car  unable to escape as batman walks toward  the wreckage  luckily penguin only has a few minor  injuries so batman and james gordon are  able to interrogate him afterward  without too much hassle so why is this  scene so troubling honestly because it's  more than a little shocking that penguin  isn't killed or at least leaving that  car in a stretcher considering how  disastrous the crash is the absurdity of  it kind of challenges our suspension of  disbelief even in a film where a grown  man dressed like a bat and acts  vigilante justice against a riddling  serial killer so why doesn't penguin die  in the batman  justice  the answer's justice it's not justice  but there are answers the first reason  is that from an effects perspective it's  just a fun cinematic way to show a car  crash you can ask the same question  about any modern action scene why  doesn't bruce wayne get whiplash when he  totals his lamborghini in the dark  knight how does anyone survive the fast  and furious movies it's about the  spectacle the other answer is even more  obvious colin farrell has more to do  with the role remember this is only the  second year of batman's crime fighting  career so there's still plenty of time  for cobblepot to become the version of  the penguin that dc fans know and love  the 2022 movie depicts him as an  up-and-coming crime boss underneath  carmine falcone and he's also in charge  of the sleazy iceberg lounge where  gotham's corrupt elite hang out most  nights  the film ends with a bit of a power  vacuum in the world of organized crime  it's highly likely that penguin will  climb the ranks to become the new crime  boss if warner brothers gives director  matt reeves green light for a sequel the  film's early reception has been  overwhelmingly positive so hopefully the  cast and crew get to come back for round  two but there's another key reason that  penguin isn't killed off in the film  he's getting his own tv series on hbo  max her variety the penguin show will be  executively produced by matt reeves  dylan clark and colin farrell hopefully  fans won't have to wait too long until  the streaming service reveals more about  what to expect from feral spin-off  series but until then we can all be glad  that this particular penguin is car  crash proof  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite bat movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

